To: <maria.ann.grimaldi@gmail.com>, <justinrill@gmail.com>


Dear Goddard Millburn Families,

We are deeply grateful for your continued trust and partnership in your
child=E2=80=99s education. It is a privilege to work alongside your family =
and to
provide a nurturing, engaging, and enriching learning environment for our
students each day.

As we prepare for the 2026=E2=80=932027 school year, we want to inform you =
that
there will be a tuition increase beginning in September 2026. As part of
our long-term planning and commitment to maintaining the quality of our
school, annual tuition adjustments are a standard practice. In past years,
tuition has typically increased by approximately 5%. This year, we are
pleased to be able to limit the increase to 4%.

This adjustment allows us to continue investing in the areas that matter
most to our families and students =E2=80=94 including attracting and retain=
ing
exceptional teachers, enhancing our programs and classroom resources, and
maintaining and improving our building and grounds to ensure a safe,
beautiful, and inspiring environment for learning.

*2026=E2=80=932027 Millburn Tuition Rates*

=E2=80=A2 Infant Classrooms (0=E2=80=9317 months): $3,005

=E2=80=A2 18 Months and Older: $2,860

For our older infants who will become toddlers during the 2026=E2=80=932027=
 school
year, tuition rates for all children in an infant classroom will be
adjusted beginning the first month the entire classroom transitions to a
toddler ratio.

*School Calendar*

Attached, you will also find our 2026=E2=80=932027 school calendar, which i=
ncludes
several thoughtful adjustments designed to better support our families,
faculty, and school community.

*Eliminating Early Closings / Additional Professional Development &
Conference Days*

One important change is the elimination of all early closing days for
professional development. Beginning next year, the school will no longer
close early for faculty training sessions. Instead, our teachers will
participate in ongoing monthly professional development through a
combination of =E2=80=9CLunch & Learn=E2=80=9D sessions and evening worksho=
ps held after
school hours.

This adjustment allows us to continue investing in our faculty while
minimizing disruption to family schedules and returning many additional
hours of care and instruction back to families throughout the year. In
exchange for these added hours, the school calendar will now include two
additional full-day closures: an added Professional Development Day in June
and a Fall Parent-Teacher Conference Day.

*Special Event Days*

Additionally, for greater ease and consistency, all special event days will
now take place on Fridays beginning at 3:00 p.m. We hope this change will
make it more convenient for parents and families to attend the many
gatherings and celebrations that help strengthen our school community and
foster family engagement.

*Parent Morning Outs*

We are also excited to expand opportunities for parents to connect and
recharge by adding several new =E2=80=9CParent Morning Out=E2=80=9D events =
in addition to
our ongoing Parent Night Out series.

*Family Handbook & Enrollment Agreement*

Also attached are our updated Family Handbook (with no major policy
changes) and Enrollment Agreement for the 2026=E2=80=932027 school year. We=
 ask
that all families review these documents carefully.

Both parents will be required to sign and return the 2026=E2=80=932027 Enro=
llment
Agreement by July 1 in order to maintain enrollment. A copy is attached
here for your convenience, and additional copies will also be available at
the school, whichever is more convenient for your family.

Please note that we continue to require a minimum of 60 days=E2=80=99 notic=
e for
student withdrawal. In addition, families of graduating students for the
2026=E2=80=932027 school year will need to notify the school of their child=
=E2=80=99s
participation in the summer program =E2=80=94 or their decision not to part=
icipate
=E2=80=94 by January 15, 2027.

*Annual Fees*

For the July tuition billing cycle, we will also include our annual fees
for the upcoming school year.

=E2=80=A2 Annual Materials Fee: $500 per student

=E2=80=A2 Flat Top-Up Deposit: $300 per student

Summer program fees for Summer 2026 will be as follows:

=C2=B7  Infants: $50

=C2=B7  Toddlers: $150

=C2=B7  Preschool: $300

=C2=B7  Children ages 4 and older attending field trips: $500

We remain deeply committed to providing the highest quality educational
experience possible and to continually strengthening the programs and
opportunities available to your children.

We sincerely appreciate your understanding, support, and partnership as we
continue to grow and invest in our school community.

Warmest regards,

Laura Kulkarni


*Millburn, NJ* - The Goddard School=C2=AE

